        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: ഒപ്പ്",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ഒപ്പ് — oppŭ — \"a signature\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ഫോമിന്റെ താഴെ നിങ്ങളുടെ ഒപ്പ് വേണം. phōminṟe tāḻe niṅṅaḷuṭe oppŭ vēṇaṁ. Your signature is needed at the bottom of the form."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "You met it in ഒപ്പിടുക, to sign: to put your ഒപ്പ് (oppŭ)."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ഒപ്പ് (oppŭ) is native Dravidian; the root means to agree or match (DEDR 924), and a signature is the mark of your agreement."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One more word for getting around."
            }
          ]
        },
